<title>USA: Philip Morris sees adverse impact from pact.</title>
<headline>Philip Morris sees adverse impact from pact.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philip Morris Cos Inc on Tuesday said a proposed litigation settlement reached between the tobacco industry and state attorneys general last week would have an adverse material impact on its financial position if enacted.</p>
<p>&quot;Implementation of the proposal would materially adversely affect the financial position of the company in the year of implementation and would likely materially adversely affect the volume, operating revenues and/or operating income of the company in future years,&quot; the company said in a filing with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission.</p>
</text>
